# OS and editor noise. The only thing that reliably tries to get itself
# committed to a repository of prose.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/

# mise: the committed config is the shared toolchain; the local one is for a
# contributor pinning something for themselves.
mise.local.toml
.mise.local.toml

# Go build output. `go build ./cmd/<x>` drops a binary in the working
# directory rather than bin/, which is how the monorepo accumulated 45 MB of
# them before anyone noticed.
bin/
*.out
*.test
coverage.*

# Catalogue artifacts are built, not committed.
*.binpb

# The assembled proto tree and the catalogue built from it (mise run assemble,
# catalogue-web). Built, never committed: the digest identifies a build.
build/

# The workspace's own sum file. go.work joins the modules for the root-level
# tasks; what a consumer builds against is each module's own go.sum, and
# `mise run acceptance` builds every module with GOWORK=off precisely so that
# the workspace cannot stand in for one. A file that only the workspace reads
# is a local artifact.
go.work.sum
